bz30l2:{w:["Have you seen products called 'eco' or 'green'? Did you believe it?","What is greenwashing?"],
 c:"Marketing has drafted an advert for new trainers. Legal counsel, Dominik, reviews it with the marketing director, Sara.",
 p:[["Sara","Marketing Director"],["Dominik","Legal Counsel"]],
 d:[[0,"So, the headline: 'Our new trainers are 100% eco-friendly and climate neutral.' Great, right?"],[1,"What exactly do you mean by 'eco-friendly'? Is there independent evidence for that?"],[0,"Well, they're made with recycled materials."],[1,"How much?"],[0,"60%."],[1,"Then 'eco-friendly' could be seen as misleading. Regulators are increasingly cracking down on vague green claims, and we'd be exposing ourselves to reputational risk."],[0,"And 'climate neutral'?"],[1,"Are we reducing emissions, or just buying offsets?"],[0,"Mostly offsets, to be honest."],[1,"Then I'd recommend we rephrase it as: 'Made with 60% recycled materials — 30% lower carbon footprint than our previous model.' This claim is backed by an independent life-cycle assessment."],[0,"Less exciting."],[1,"But credible. We'd rather under-promise and over-deliver. And we offset only what we cannot yet reduce — we can say that honestly."]],
 q:[["What's the problem with 'eco-friendly'?","It's vague and could be misleading.","It's too long.","It's illegal everywhere.","Nothing.",0],["How much recycled material do the trainers have?","60%","100%","30%","10%",0],["Why is 'climate neutral' a problem?","It's mostly based on offsets, not reductions.","It's not in English.","It's too technical.","Customers don't understand.",0],["What backs the new claim?","An independent life-cycle assessment","The marketing team","Customer reviews","Nothing",0]],
 f:[["Our product is eco.","Our product is made with 60% recycled materials.",["recycled","made with"]],["Sustainable? Sure, OK.","What exactly do you mean by 'sustainable'?",["what exactly do you mean"]],["This ad is a lie.","That claim could be seen as misleading.",["could be seen as misleading"]],["We're 100% green now!","We're not there yet, but we're making progress.",["not there yet"]]],
 r:{h:"Challenge a green claim",s:"A colleague wants to publish a vague green claim. Ask for precision and evidence, explain the risk and propose a specific, honest alternative.",b:["Ask what exactly they mean","Ask for evidence","Explain legal and reputational risk","Rephrase it specifically"]},
 wr:{h:"Comment on the ad draft",s:"Write a comment to Marketing on an ad that says 'Our coffee is 100% sustainable'. Explain the risks and suggest two honest alternatives.",to:"marketing@company.com",su:"Ad draft — sustainability claim",min:110}},

bz30l3:{w:["Have you ever faced an ethical dilemma at work?","Is it OK to accept gifts from suppliers? Where's the line?"],
 c:"A supplier has offered the procurement director, Adam, a weekend in Dubai for him and his wife if the company signs a contract. He discusses it with his manager, Helena.",
 p:[["Adam","Procurement Director"],["Helena","Chief Operating Officer"]],
 d:[[0,"Helena, the supplier has offered me a weekend in Dubai if we sign. It's legal — no rule says I can't accept."],[1,"Just because it's legal doesn't mean it's right. I'm uncomfortable with that."],[0,"Everyone in the industry does it."],[1,"This could constitute a conflict of interest. How would this look if it were on the front page?"],[0,"Not great, I suppose."],[1,"Were we to accept, we'd be setting a dangerous precedent. Who else would be affected by this decision?"],[0,"The other suppliers who bid. And our team, I guess."],[1,"Exactly. The short-term gain isn't worth the long-term risk."],[0,"So what do I do?"],[1,"I'd suggest we consult compliance before you reply, and we should declare this openly. On balance, I think you should decline politely."],[0,"And the contract itself?"],[1,"We decide it on price and quality alone — as if the offer had never been made. Should you have any doubts, compliance is there to help."]],
 q:[["What has the supplier offered?","A weekend in Dubai","A discount","A job","A new car",0],["What test does Helena suggest?","The front-page test","A legal test","A price test","A vote",0],["Who else would be affected?","Other suppliers who bid, and the team","Nobody","Only Adam's wife","The bank",0],["What does Helena recommend?","Consult compliance, declare it, decline politely","Accept quietly","Ask for more","Cancel the contract",0]],
 f:[["It's legal, so OK.","Just because it's legal doesn't mean it's right.",["just because it's legal"]],["If we take it, problem later.","Were we to accept, we'd be setting a dangerous precedent.",["were we to accept","dangerous precedent"]],["I think no.","On balance, I think we should decline.",["on balance"]],["If you have problems, call compliance.","Should you have any doubts, compliance is there to help.",["should you have"]]],
 r:{h:"Discuss an ethical dilemma",s:"A colleague is tempted by something legal but questionable (a gift, a misleading report, hiding a mistake). Raise your concern, apply the front-page test, weigh stakeholders and recommend a course of action.",b:["Raise the concern respectfully","Use the front-page test and 'legal ≠ right'","Consider stakeholders and precedent","Recommend action, using an inverted conditional"]},
 wr:{h:"Declaration to compliance",s:"Write Adam's email to compliance declaring the offer, explaining that he will decline, and asking how to reply to the supplier.",to:"compliance@company.com",su:"Declaration: hospitality offer from supplier",min:110}}
